In the directory `/tmp/sv-25bc41f6da8c4ee9862d791a01a69806/before`, fix several special-case AOT compatibility issues.

## 1. Fix ManagedServiceIdentity.Serialization.cs (Custom JsonConverter case)

File: `Common/Custom/Models/ManagedServiceIdentity.Serialization.cs`

This file has these problematic calls:
- Line 31: `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions)` — This uses the `ManagedServiceIdentityTypeConverter` which writes `"type": "value"`. Replace it with the converter logic directly:
  ```csharp
  writer.WritePropertyName("type"u8);
  writer.WriteStringValue(ManagedServiceIdentityType.ToString());
  ```

- Line 49: `JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions)` — `item.Value` is a `UserAssignedIdentity` which implements `IJsonModel<UserAssignedIdentity>`. Replace with:
  ```csharp
  writer.WriteObjectValue(item.Value, options);
  ```
  (Note: `options` is the `ModelReaderWriterOptions` parameter of the `Write` method)

- Line 206: `type = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}");` — This parses `{"type": "SomeValue"}` using the converter. Replace with direct parsing logic:
  ```csharp
  type = new ManagedServiceIdentityType(property.Value.GetString());
  ```

- Line 218: `dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), JsonSerializer.Deserialize<UserAssignedIdentity>(property0.Value.GetRawText()));` — Replace with:
  ```csharp
  dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), UserAssignedIdentity.DeserializeUserAssignedIdentity(property0.Value));
  ```

Also, the `jOptions` parameter in the `Write` method (line 22) is no longer needed. BUT don't change the method signature since it's called from line 58 `Write(writer, options, null)` — just leave the parameter but it won't be used. Actually leave the signature as-is since it's an `internal` method.

## 2. Fix ArmEnvironment.ToString()

File: `ArmEnvironment.cs`

Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Replace with a manual implementation that doesn't use reflection:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
}
```

## 3. Fix ArmClientOptions.SetApiVersionsFromProfile()

File: `ArmClientOptions.cs`

Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

